---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import StatusBadge from '@/components/StatusBadge.astro';
import SourceBadge from '@/components/SourceBadge.astro';
import LicenseBadge from '@/components/LicenseBadge.astro';
import { STATUSES, SOURCE_STATUSES } from '@/content/schema';
import { STATUS_INFO, SOURCE_INFO, LICENSE_SENTINELS } from '@/lib/labels';
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="What altstrument lists, what it does not, how to read the badges, and how to contribute."
  editPath="src/pages/about.astro"
>
  <h1 class="text-2xl">About</h1>

  <div class="mt-4 flex max-w-[68ch] flex-col gap-8 [&_h2]:mb-2 [&_h2]:text-lg [&_p+p]:mt-3">
    <section aria-labelledby="what">
      <h2 id="what">What this is</h2>
      <p>
        altstrument is a directory of custom and third-party firmware and tools for music hardware. Entries are grouped by
        device and then by firmware project. Each one records the authors, where the source lives, the license, and the
        version history, so you can tell who made something, whether you can read it, and how recently it was touched.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="scope">
      <h2 id="scope">Scope</h2>
      <p>
        The catalog covers grooveboxes, synths, samplers, drum machines, controllers, pedals, Eurorack modules, vintage
        gear, and DIY platforms. Host-side tools that support a scene, such as editors, flashers, emulators and SDKs,
        are listed alongside the firmware they serve.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="policy">
      <h2 id="policy">Policy</h2>
      <p>
        We link; we never host firmware binaries. We also never link to redistributed copies of manufacturer firmware.
        Where a project works by patching a stock file, you supply that file yourself from the manufacturer.
      </p>
      <p>
        Entries carrying a brick-risk flag have a known, documented risk of damaging the device. Flashing third-party
        firmware may void your warranty, and doing so is at your own risk. Read the project's own notes before you
        start, and keep a way back to stock where one exists.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="badges">
      <h2 id="badges">Reading the badges</h2>
      <p class="mb-3">Status describes how alive the project is.</p>
      <dl class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-4 gap-y-2 sm:grid-cols-[max-content_1fr]">
        {STATUSES.map((s) => (
          <>
            <dt><StatusBadge status={s} /></dt>
            <dd class="mb-2 sm:mb-0">{STATUS_INFO[s].desc}</dd>
          </>
        ))}
      </dl>
      <p class="mb-3 mt-5">Source describes how much of the work is public.</p>
      <dl class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-4 gap-y-2 sm:grid-cols-[max-content_1fr]">
        {SOURCE_STATUSES.map((s) => (
          <>
            <dt><SourceBadge status={s} /></dt>
            <dd class="mb-2 sm:mb-0">{SOURCE_INFO[s].desc}</dd>
          </>
        ))}
      </dl>
      <p class="mb-3 mt-5">
        License is an <a href="https://spdx.org/licenses/" rel="noopener">SPDX</a> identifier linking to the license
        text. Two values are not licenses in that sense and appear as plain, muted badges.
      </p>
      <dl class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-4 gap-y-2 sm:grid-cols-[max-content_1fr]">
        {Object.entries(LICENSE_SENTINELS).map(([id, desc]) => (
          <>
            <dt><LicenseBadge license={id} /></dt>
            <dd class="mb-2 sm:mb-0">{desc}</dd>
          </>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="contribute">
      <h2 id="contribute">Contributing</h2>
      <p>
        The catalog is plain YAML. To add or correct an entry, open a pull request that adds or edits a file under
        <code>src/content</code>: one file per device in <code>devices/</code>, and one per firmware project in
        <code>firmwares/&lt;device&gt;/</code>. A validator checks the schema on every build. See
        <code>CONTRIBUTING.md</code> in the repository for the field reference and the rules about omitting dates
        rather than guessing them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="api">
      <h2 id="api">Data and API</h2>
      <p>The whole catalog is available as static files, rebuilt on every change:</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5">
        <li><a href="/api/catalog.json">/api/catalog.json</a>: every manufacturer, device, firmware and version as JSON</li>
        <li><a href="/api/stats.json">/api/stats.json</a>: device, firmware and tool counts</li>
        <li><a href="/feed.xml">/feed.xml</a>: RSS feed of the most recent dated versions</li>
        <li><a href="/sitemap-index.xml">/sitemap-index.xml</a>: every page on the site</li>
        <li><a href="/.well-known/api-catalog">/.well-known/api-catalog</a>: the JSON endpoints above as an RFC 9727 API catalog</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="thanks">
      <h2 id="thanks">Prior art and thanks</h2>
      <p>This site builds on lists others have kept for years:</p>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5">
        <li><code>Lapin/awesome-music-gear-firmware</code></li>
        <li><code>aroum/fm1-custom-fw</code></li>
        <li><code>Maxhodges/noise-engineering-firmware-index</code></li>
        <li>Mutable Instruments' third-party firmware page</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="license">
      <h2 id="license">Licensing</h2>
      <p>
        The site code is released under the MIT license. The catalog data is released under
        <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" rel="noopener">CC-BY-4.0</a>; reuse it with attribution.
        A full JSON export is listed under <a href="#api">Data and API</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Device images are the manufacturers' own product and press photos, shown with attribution and a link to
        where they are published. They remain the property of their owners and are not covered by the catalog's
        CC-BY-4.0 license. Where no product image is available, the manufacturer's logo is shown instead; those are
        public-domain wordmarks or brand assets used with permission, and remain trademarks of their owners. If you
        own an image or mark shown here and want it changed or removed, open an issue.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
